             '<b>The mean is not moderation for its own sake.</b> The courageous response can be intense, and the generous response can be large. The target is relative to us and the case, set by the practically wise person. That makes the theory useful for a founder choosing between cowardly avoidance and reckless expansion, but it also leaves hard judgement work unresolved.',
